#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CHNSetti 1.0.0 — native CHNS processing, visual integration and calibration review.

Instrument: Thermo Scientific Flash 2000 Organic Elemental Analyzer (CHNS-O) with
Eager 300 software. Eager 300 writes, into one run folder: the .MTH method and
sample table (with the element identification table), one .DAT per analysis
(detector signal plus the saved integration), the .SUM summary, the .EAM file
and cc.cc, a CFR21_11 log of when each file was last saved.

Open a method with its same-folder DAT detector records; SUM is optional.
Automatic proposals and manual boundary/baseline edits use unsmoothed detector
signals. Calibration standards and samples use the same numerical integration
policy. Models include averaged K, origin least squares and fitted intercept.
Original saved signals/results remain intact. Explicit processing decisions,
reviewed zeros, point exclusions, revisions and their reasons are retained.
An element without a peak (neither in the instrument's saved integration nor in an applied CHNSetti
integration) is reported as 0, following the laboratory's convention (0, not NQ); the audit keeps it as
not quantified.

Dependencies: PySide6 and openpyxl; xlrd is optional. NumPy and SciPy are not needed.
Build the Windows executable on Windows with the included build helper.
License GPL-3.0. XLS BIFF8 fallback adapted from the author's Plasmatti.
"""
